# API and Data Fetching Rules

## 🌐 API Architecture

### Request Utility Structure

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Use utils/request.ts
import request from "@utils/request";

const response = await request<RequestType, ResponseType, ErrorType>({
  uri: "/api/endpoint",
  method: "get",
  data: requestData,
});
```

### Query Organization

```
query/
├── get/           # GET requests
├── post/          # POST requests
├── patch/         # PATCH requests
├── delete/        # DELETE requests
└── index.ts       # Exports
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** use the centralized request utility
✅ **ALWAYS** create proper TypeScript interfaces for API responses
✅ **ALWAYS** use TanStack Query for data fetching
✅ **ALWAYS** handle loading, error, and success states
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper error boundaries
✅ **ALWAYS** use query keys for caching
✅ **ALWAYS** set appropriate staleTime and cacheTime
✅ **ALWAYS** use proper HTTP methods (GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE)

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** use fetch or axios directly in components
❌ **NEVER** forget to handle API errors
❌ **NEVER** create queries without proper TypeScript types
❌ **NEVER** use any type for API responses
❌ **NEVER** forget to invalidate queries after mutations
❌ **NEVER** make API calls in render functions

### Query Hook Template

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Query hook structure
import { useQuery } from "@tanstack/react-query";
import { QUERY_KEYS } from "@constants/keys";
import request from "@utils/request";

interface UserData {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
}

function useGetUser(userId: number) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: [QUERY_KEYS.GET_USER, userId],
    queryFn: async () => {
      const response = await request<null, UserData, null>({
        uri: `/api/users/${userId}`,
        method: "get",
      });
      return response.data;
    },
    staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000, // 5 minutes
    retry: 1,
  });
}
```

### Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Error handling in components
function UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: number }) {
  const { data: user, isLoading, error } = useGetUser(userId);

  if (isLoading) return <Loading />;
  if (error) return <ErrorMessage error={error} />;
  if (!user) return <NotFound />;

  return <UserCard user={user} />;
}
```

